I've been playing Nethack and Slash'EM on and off for a few years now,
and I've never really been very good at it - my best game ever saw me
getting slaughtered by Master Kaen at the bottom of the Monk Quest
dungeon, and it seems likely that it was pure luck on my part.

Recently, however, I've begun to slow things down a bit and abandon
the "charge forward and melee everything that moves, then take their
stuff" technique in favor of a more cautious and deliberate one.  As
such, I've seen it become very common to reach MineTown or the Oracle,
whereas previously I'd generally be overwhelmed by numbers a few
levels into the dungeon at least half the time.

